Proactively analysed custom code for JDK 17 with Red Hat Migration Toolkit, automated JBoss PicketBox‑to‑Elytron configuration, and reverse‑engineered alert processor to REST JSON, de‑risking platform modernisation.

Description (997 characters)

Months before the official JDK 8→17 migration, I scanned all custom Finacle code using the Red Hat Migration Toolkit, identifying deprecated APIs and threading changes. I triaged findings and prioritised code‑compatibility work, giving the team weeks of advance readiness when the vendor’s migration pattern arrived. To eliminate hours of manual JBoss 7 configuration, I built an Ansible suite that automates the full PicketBox‑to‑Elytron migration: creating credential stores with encrypted DB aliases, updating standalone XML and JVM parameters per environment. Setup time reduced from 4 hours to under 15 minutes with zero drift. When the alert event processor source code was missing for the BI SOAP‑to‑REST modernisation, I decompiled the class files, reverse‑engineered the logic, and implemented JSON REST alerting. I tested thoroughly, unblocking BI’s critical dependency. These automations were handed off as part of the official migration runbook, directly accelerating the transition.

Impact (246 characters)

Prevented ~3 weeks of reactive JDK debugging. JBoss environment provisioning now 15 min, error‑free. Alert processor delivered ahead of vendor schedule, keeping BI modernisation on track. Migration risk significantly reduced; runbook reused as team standard for all future environments.

