Title (198 characters)

Centralised pre‑prod automation via Git‑Ansible sync, led Python 3.6→3.12 migration, built Datadog event metrics, and hardened pipelines with ^M validation, DB unlock job, expanded smoke tests and auto‑refresh tracking.

Description (1,000 characters)

I built a single Git repository as the source of truth for all platform scripts, monitors and configurations. Using my Ansible playbooks, any approved change now synchronises to all dev and ESQM regions in minutes, eliminating years of manual drift. I led the Python 3.6.8 to 3.12 migration—scanning the entire codebase, refactoring deprecated constructs, testing on RHELCERT, and rolling out with zero monitoring gaps. I created custom Datadog metrics tracking real‑time Finacle event processing volumes, validated them on RHELCERT and deployed to production. To harden pipelines, I added a ^M character pre‑validation that caught three bad patches before they could delay batches; expanded the smoke‑test suite to cover account origination and SR creation; built an Ansible job for one‑click DB user unlocks; and modified the refresh pipeline to auto‑capture change numbers, data sources and patch details into a database, eliminating manual trackers. I also fine‑tuned over 200 monitors, muting non‑critical alerts and reducing noise by 60%.

